WEBVTT

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:07.719
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twentieth, here we go. Can you all hear me on Teams?</v>

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:16.829
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, sadly. Already discussing next weekend's plans at ours. Supposed to be barbecue weather, but that was the forecast for yesterday and we got soaked.</v>

00:00:17.829 --> 00:00:20.980
<v Callum Reid>British summer, mate. Barbecue under an umbrella, perfectly normal.</v>

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:28.420
<v Marcus Hale>And the coffee machine in the canteen's still broken. Just a moan, not putting that on anyone's list.</v>

00:00:29.879 --> 00:00:35.829
<v Fiona Doyle>Between that and the traffic on the ring road, lovely start. I barely moved for twenty minutes.</v>

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.070
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we all go home again—finished bits first?</v>

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:48.250
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah so, tested the GT2 yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done, nothing left over from that.</v>

00:00:49.259 --> 00:00:52.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Nice to have one that's actually closed.</v>

00:00:53.299 --> 00:00:58.899
<v Marcus Hale>And I signed off the inspection on the CT1 on Tuesday. Last Tuesday, obviously. Already finished.</v>

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.909
<v Hannah Price>Yep, understood. Not another inspection for today.</v>

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.000
<v Sarah Okafor>Blockers haven't shifted: can't get to the Waste Heat Boiler until production gives us a window. That work's still blocked.</v>

00:01:11.569 --> 00:01:17.519
<v Callum Reid>Same story on the big boiler. Still waiting on parts, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.680
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, both still blocked, not pretending they're available work.</v>

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:30.890
<v Marcus Hale>And the shutdown on the water booster is cancelled now, production need it running. That's off, not postponed into today's list.</v>

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:35.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. We're not reopening that shutdown here.</v>

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:44.230
<v Marcus Hale>While I've got the mic, heard a slight rattle from the wrapper. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:01:46.469 --> 00:01:53.120
<v Fiona Doyle>Similar from me: heard a slight rattle from the GT1 Compressor Section. Nothing to action yet on that either.</v>

00:01:55.439 --> 00:01:59.290
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, observations only. Neither's a new job out of this meeting.</v>

00:02:01.129 --> 00:02:07.079
<v Grace Liu>What about writing up the near miss at the relief valve? That still needs doing, doesn't it?</v>

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:17.919
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes. I'll write up the near miss at the relief valve by the end of the week. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:23.000
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, Saz. That's the one causing us grief, yeah.</v>

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:29.099
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, mine. First thing on my list, not something I'm leaving until everything else is done.</v>

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:37.439
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you grease and check the bearings on the Water Booster Pump tomorrow at 9:30, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:44.599
<v Hannah Price>Just the bearings scope on the Water Booster Pump, yeah? Not taking on that cancelled shutdown as well.</v>

00:02:46.169 --> 00:02:50.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, just grease and check the bearings. The shutdown remains cancelled.</v>

00:02:50.379 --> 00:02:57.729
<v Hannah Price>Okay, I'll grease and check the bearings on the Water Booster Pump tomorrow at 9:30. Got you on the spare-minute priority.</v>

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.560
<v Marcus Hale>Han's got the glamorous one, then.</v>

00:03:02.639 --> 00:03:04.389
<v Hannah Price>Oh, absolutely. Living the dream.</v>

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.860
<v Sarah Okafor>Grace, can you run the monthly fire alarm test tomorrow? Fairly important, that one.</v>

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:15.219
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll run the monthly fire alarm test tomorrow. Fairly important, understood.</v>

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:18.699
<v Callum Reid>Sorry, you clipped a bit there—monthly test?</v>

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:23.280
<v Grace Liu>Monthly test, yes. That's the one Saz just asked for.</v>

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:32.400
<v Fiona Doyle>There's also the toolbox talk for the team. Someone needs to organise it today; it's fairly important. Has that actually got anyone against it?</v>

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:38.509
<v Grace Liu>Not me, sorry. I haven't got capacity to take the organising on.</v>

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:42.550
<v Callum Reid>I can't take that either. Sorry, talking over you there.</v>

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:50.409
<v Sarah Okafor>No worries. So organising the toolbox talk for the team is needed today, fairly important, but nobody's taken it. It's unallocated.</v>

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:53.969
<v Fiona Doyle>Right. Raising the gap, not volunteering myself for it.</v>

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:59.840
<v Aisha Begum>On my side, I'll replace the seals on the turbine two water valve this afternoon.</v>

00:04:01.389 --> 00:04:06.289
<v Marcus Hale>The seals, rather than the whole valve? Sorry, just making sure I heard that.</v>

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:12.460
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, the seals on the turbine two water valve. I'll do those this afternoon.</v>

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:20.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Aisha, can you also take vibration readings on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel at half two? Top priority please.</v>

00:04:22.439 --> 00:04:28.740
<v Aisha Begum>Yes, I'll take vibration readings on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel at half two. Top priority, understood.</v>

00:04:30.709 --> 00:04:35.259
<v Fiona Doyle>Does that clash with the seals, or is the afternoon wording loose enough?</v>

00:04:36.689 --> 00:04:43.689
<v Aisha Begum>It's fine. The seals are this afternoon; half two is the fixed time for the readings. I can keep both.</v>

00:04:45.959 --> 00:04:51.560
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, Aisha. The Line 3 Screw and Barrel readings are the top priority of those, please.</v>

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:58.569
<v Aisha Begum>And I'll schedule downtime for the boiler safety valve with production next Tuesday. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:05.350
<v Callum Reid>That's the scheduling with production, yeah? Not saying the valve work itself is happening next Tuesday.</v>

00:05:07.819 --> 00:05:16.569
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. I'll schedule the downtime for the boiler safety valve with production next Tuesday. I'm not promising a work date off the back of that.</v>

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:22.459
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, that distinction makes sense. Scheduling, not an agreed outage yet.</v>

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:30.839
<v Aisha Begum>While we're on next Tuesday, I'll do a site visit at Harbour Road Warehouse with the contractor next Tuesday as well.</v>

00:05:33.209 --> 00:05:37.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Aisha, you're taking the Harbour Road Warehouse site visit with the contractor?</v>

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:40.259
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, I'll do it. Next Tuesday.</v>

00:05:40.879 --> 00:05:42.980
<v Fiona Doyle>Your calendar's earning its keep, then.</v>

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:47.769
<v Aisha Begum>For once it's more than coloured squares. Those two fit, yeah.</v>

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:54.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Fi, can you send the shift handover report round? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:56.199 --> 00:06:01.100
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round. Matters but isn't urgent, got it.</v>

00:06:02.769 --> 00:06:07.670
<v Callum Reid>Useful having the same report in front of everyone rather than half a conversation.</v>

00:06:09.199 --> 00:06:13.050
<v Fiona Doyle>Exactly. And I've heard you on the priority, Saz—no panic attached.</v>

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:18.649
<v Marcus Hale>Unlike the coffee situation, which feels very urgent to me personally.</v>

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:22.290
<v Grace Liu>Still not a work order, however emotionally significant.</v>

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:26.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. Anything in what we've agreed that someone hasn't understood?</v>

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:34.850
<v Callum Reid>No. And the blocked boiler bits are still blocked, just so silence doesn't sound like they've magically cleared.</v>

00:06:35.730 --> 00:06:43.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. Only ownership gap we've raised is organising the toolbox talk for the team today. Fairly important, still nobody on it.</v>

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:45.490
<v Fiona Doyle>Agreed. No name against that one.</v>

00:06:46.899 --> 00:06:48.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>
